{{ if .Options.auto_attach -}}
- Every new interactive shell outside tmux attaches to the tmux session `{{ .Options.session }}`, or creates it if it does not exist yet
- Inside tmux (`$TMUX` is set) nothing happens
- Without `tmux` installed the shell starts normally
{{ else -}}
- Nothing starts automatically (`auto_attach` is false); run `tmux` yourself
{{ end -}}
- `tmux ls` — list sessions
- Default key bindings (this module ships no tmux config); press `Ctrl-b` first, then:
  - `Ctrl-b d` — detach; the session keeps running
  - `Ctrl-b c` — new window; `Ctrl-b n` / `Ctrl-b p` — next / previous window
  - `Ctrl-b %` — split left/right; `Ctrl-b "` — split top/bottom
  - `Ctrl-b [` — copy mode (scroll back through the output)
  - `Ctrl-b ?` — list all key bindings
